{"file":"Atlassian Forge Skills-0.1.0-v2.zip","bytes":176447,"status":"已读取","plugins":[{"path":".claude-plugin/plugin.json","name":"forge-skills","description":"Forge app builder skill bundle with Forge MCP configuration for Atlassian Forge workflows.","version":"0.1.0"},{"path":".codex-plugin/plugin.json","name":"forge-skills","description":"Forge app builder skill bundle with Forge MCP integration for Atlassian Forge workflows.","version":"0.1.0"},{"path":".cursor-plugin/plugin.json","name":"forge-skills","displayName":"Forge Skills","description":"Forge app builder skill bundle with Forge MCP integration for building, deploying, and troubleshooting Atlassian Forge apps.","version":"0.1.0","license":"Apache-2.0","repository":"https://github.com/atlassian/forge-skills.git","homepage":"https://developer.atlassian.com/platform/forge/","keywords":["forge","atlassian","jira","confluence","mcp","skills"]},{"path":".plugin/plugin.json","name":"forge-skills","description":"Forge app builder skill bundle with Forge MCP integration for Atlassian Forge workflows.","version":"0.1.0","license":"Apache-2.0","repository":"https://github.com/atlassian/forge-skills.git","homepage":"https://github.com/atlassian/forge-skills","keywords":["forge","atlassian","jira","confluence","mcp","skills"]},{"path":"plugin.json","name":"forge-skills","description":"Forge app builder skill bundle with Forge MCP integration for Atlassian Forge workflows.","version":"0.1.0","license":"Apache-2.0","repository":"https://github.com/atlassian/forge-skills.git","homepage":"https://github.com/atlassian/forge-skills","keywords":["forge","atlassian","jira","confluence","mcp","skills"]}],"skills":[{"path":"skills/forge-app-builder/SKILL.md","name":"forge-app-builder","description":"Plan, build, scaffold, or safely extend Atlassian Forge apps using current official documentation. Use for fresh Forge apps, existing-app feature work, module and manifest changes, UI Kit or Custom UI implementation, backend functions and events, Atlassian or external APIs, storage, permissions, environment configuration, distribution-affecting implementation, validation, and explicitly authorized deployment or installation; route standalone debugging and specialist reviews to their dedicated skills.","headings":["Forge App Builder","Preserve these invariants","Route the primary intent","Ground the selected route","Activate capability gates conditionally","Implement and validate iteratively","Validate and stop safely"],"name_hint":"forge · app · builder"},{"path":"skills/forge-app-review/SKILL.md","name":"forge-app-review","description":"Performs a lightweight pre-release readiness review of Atlassian Forge apps across manifest/module wiring, architecture, runtime compatibility, dependency posture, tests, deploy readiness, and obvious security, cost, or reliability smells. Use when the user asks \"review my Forge app\", \"pre-deploy check\", \"is this app ready to ship\", \"review manifest\", \"general app review\", \"release readiness\", or asks for a broad quality pass. Do not use for deep security audits/SAST/exploitability review, cost optimization, or diagnosing a known broken app; route those to forge-security-review, forge-cost-optimizer, or forge-debugger respectively.","headings":["Forge App Review","Boundaries","Review Rules","Module & Capability Routing","Workflow","What To Check","Release Blockers","Architecture And Maintainability","Lightweight Security Signals","Lightweight Cost Signals","Lightweight Debuggability Signals","Output Format","Forge App Review Results","Summary","Findings","Clean Areas","Suggested Next Step"],"name_hint":"forge · app · 评审"},{"path":"skills/forge-connector/SKILL.md","name":"forge-connector","description":"Guides building and deploying Atlassian Forge Teamwork Graph connector apps that ingest external data into Atlassian's Teamwork Graph, making it searchable in Rovo Search and surfaced in Rovo Chat. Use when the user wants to build a Forge connector, ingest external data into Atlassian, connect a third-party tool (e.g. Google Drive, ServiceNow, Salesforce) to Atlassian, make external content searchable in Rovo, build a graph:connector module, use the @forge/teamwork-graph SDK, or implement onConnectionChange / validateConnection functions.","headings":["Forge Connector","Critical Rules","MCP Prerequisites","Agent Workflow — Complete Steps 0–7 in Order","Step 0: Prerequisites","Step 1: Discover Developer Spaces","Step 1.5: Discover Data & Map to Object Types","Step 2: Scaffold the Connector App","Step 3: Customize the Generated Code","Step 4: Deploy and Install","Derive forge-app-builder skill dir from this SKILL.md's path:","e.g. if this file is at /path/to/skills/forge-connector/SKILL.md","then the deploy script dir is: /path/to/skills/forge-app-builder/","If you have the site URL:","If you don't have the site URL yet, deploy first then ask:","Ask: \"What is your Atlassian site URL (e.g. yourcompany.atlassian.net)?\"","Step 5: Connect via Atlassian Administration","Step 6: Monitor with forge tunnel"],"name_hint":"forge · 连接器"},{"path":"skills/forge-cost-optimizer/SKILL.md","name":"forge-cost-optimizer","description":"Optimizes Atlassian Forge apps to reduce platform consumption and avoid unnecessary costs using Atlassian's \"Optimise Forge platform costs\" guidance. Use when the user asks to optimize Forge app costs, reduce Forge invocations, lower GB-seconds, reduce storage or log usage, tune memory, replace polling, improve scheduled triggers, reduce KVS writes, move work to the frontend, use bridge APIs, batch API calls, add caching, or evaluate Forge Remote trade-offs. By default, perform an audit first and offer to make the recommended changes after presenting the audit. Only modify files immediately when the user explicitly asks the agent to implement or apply optimizations.","headings":["Forge Cost Optimizer","Source Guidance","Core Principle","When Triggered","Optimization Workflow","Step 1: Establish the Cost Profile","Step 2: Find No-Invocation Opportunities","Step 3: Optimize Triggers and Scheduling","Step 4: Optimize API and Data Fetching","Step 5: Optimize Storage","Step 6: Optimize Logging","Step 7: Tune Function Memory","Step 8: Evaluate Forge Remote Carefully","Safe Implementation Patterns","Finding Patterns Quickly","Output Format","Forge Cost Optimization Audit","Summary"],"name_hint":"forge · 成本 · optimizer"},{"path":"skills/forge-debugger/SKILL.md","name":"forge-debugger","description":"Diagnoses and fixes issues in Atlassian Forge apps. Use this skill whenever a Forge app has errors, crashes, shows blank UI, fails to deploy, doesn't appear after installation, has permission issues, or produces unexpected output. Trigger on any mention of forge logs, forge deploy errors, resolver errors, blank panels, missing scopes, Custom UI not rendering, production vs dev discrepancies, or any Jira/Confluence app that \"stopped working\". Also trigger when the user asks to debug, troubleshoot, investigate, or fix a Forge app issue — even if they haven't used the word \"Forge\" but describe a Jira panel or Confluence macro acting up.","headings":["Forge App Debugger","EXECUTION MANDATE","Diagnostic Principles","Step 1: Classify the Error","Step 2: Version Check","Step 3: Lint","Step 4: Custom UI Build Check","Step 5: Deploy Status","Step 6: Logs","If no logs are returned","If the error is in the frontend (UI rendering, blank screen)","Step 7: Production Issues","Common Error Patterns","Handler Path Resolution","Invoke Name vs Function Key","API Migration (v1 → v2)","Step 8: Cleanup","Escalation"],"name_hint":"forge · debugger"},{"path":"skills/forge-security-review/SKILL.md","name":"forge-security-review","description":"Performs a white-box security review of Atlassian Forge apps using structured, Forge-specific security rules and evidence-driven reporting. Use when the user asks for a Forge security review, security audit, vuln assessment, pentest-style code review, authz review, tenant isolation analysis, web trigger hardening, or static analysis execution for a Forge app.","headings":["Forge Security Review","Token-Efficient Default","Rule Assets","Execution Mandate","Rule Routing Workflow","Phase 1: Reconnaissance (Mandatory)","Phase 2: Index Rule Selection (Two-Tier Loading)","Phase 3: Analysis and Verification","Focused Review Mode","Review Workflow","Static Analysis Mode","Output Requirements","Example Trigger Phrases"],"name_hint":"forge · 安全 · 评审"}],"commands":[],"readmes":[{"path":"README.md","headings":["Atlassian Forge Skills","What's included","Skills","Forge MCP Server","ADS MCP Server","Prerequisites","Install","Claude Code","Cursor","Gemini CLI","GitHub Copilot CLI","OpenAI Codex","Kiro and Agent Plugins clients","Rovo Dev","Verify the installation","1. Verify the skill layer","2. Verify Forge MCP","3. Verify ADS MCP (Custom UI only)","4. Verify Forge Connector skill","Prompts to try","What you get","Authentication","Troubleshooting","The agent is not using Forge skills","MCP tools are not showing up","Forge commands fail with auth errors","forge create fails","Learn more","Contributing","License"]},{"path":"skills/forge-debugger/README.md","headings":["Forge Debugger Skill","Use For","Do Not Use For","Specialist Handoffs","What It Checks","Debugging Flow","Example Prompts"]},{"path":"skills/forge-connector/README.md","headings":["Forge Connector Skill","What This Skill Does","Prerequisites","Quick Start","From the forge-connector skill directory:","Object Types Indexed in Rovo Search","SDK Reference","Scripts","Further Reading"]},{"path":"skills/forge-app-review/README.md","headings":["Forge App Review Skill","Use For","Do Not Use For","Specialist Handoffs","What It Checks","Example Prompts"]},{"path":"skills/forge-app-builder/README.md","headings":["Forge App Builder Skill","Installation","Using only this skill folder (advanced)","What This Skill Provides"]},{"path":"skills/forge-cost-optimizer/README.md","